WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:04.000
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

00:04.170 --> 00:06.000
It's not here... Or here!

00:06.920 --> 00:08.210
I'm home, Elda!

00:09.920 --> 00:11.580
Koma-chan tagged along today!

00:11.830 --> 00:14.880
I've got lots of time today. Anything interesting going on?

00:15.170 --> 00:18.710
Y-you're both right on time!
Something awful has happened!

00:18.710 --> 00:20.920
A burglar may have broken in!

00:21.000 --> 00:22.500
What?! A burglar?!

00:22.500 --> 00:24.080
Is there something missing?!

00:24.580 --> 00:33.330
The HG 1/144 Mobile Warrior Gongem 35th Anniversary
Limited Edition Clear Version is missing!

00:34.290 --> 00:36.460
<b>IT'S MY PRIZED POSSESSION!</b>

00:37.920 --> 00:38.750
What'd you say?

00:38.920 --> 00:45.670
I said, the HG 1/144 Mobile Warrior Gongem 35th
Anniversary Limited Edition Clear Ver-

00:40.380 --> 00:45.710
<b>HG 1/144 Mobile Warrior Gongem 35th Anniversary Limited Edition Clear Version</b>

02:15.790 --> 02:20.380
<b>EPISODE 11</b>

02:15.790 --> 02:20.380
<b>DETECTIVE</b>

02:15.790 --> 02:20.380
<b>KOMA-CHAN</b>

02:17.250 --> 02:19.670
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

02:20.330 --> 02:24.670
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

02:22.330 --> 02:25.290
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

02:25.460 --> 02:29.540
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

02:30.210 --> 02:32.460
...was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

02:34.290 --> 02:36.000
A limited edition plastic model?

02:36.250 --> 02:37.960
Was it a rare one?

02:38.380 --> 02:42.920
Y-yeah... It's a model that only had
a handful produced 5 years ago,

02:42.920 --> 02:45.580
and it's so rare that you can't get one nowadays.

02:45.880 --> 02:50.630
I wanted to play with it since it's been awhile,
but I've looked everywhere and can't find it.

02:51.040 --> 02:54.460
A rare plastic model, huh? Hmm...

02:55.920 --> 03:00.420
Is it not in your closet? I mean,
we organized your closet together the other day.

03:00.630 --> 03:06.420
N-no, I looked in the closet and the warehouse,
but it wasn't in either of those places!

03:06.540 --> 03:10.670
Well, there isn't a burglar alive
that only steals plastic models.

03:10.880 --> 03:15.880
Don't be so sure about that. These days even
plastic models are sold at an unbelievable premium.

03:16.040 --> 03:20.000
Th-then it really was stolen?! Th-this is awful!

03:20.250 --> 03:22.080
Wh-wh-what'll I do?!

03:22.210 --> 03:24.250
I have to buy a safe to put all of my rare toys in!

03:24.630 --> 03:27.960
And then I have to buy a big vault to put that vault in!

03:28.380 --> 03:30.670
P-police! Call the police!

03:30.670 --> 03:33.790
Ah, but I don't want them to come into my room!

03:34.080 --> 03:35.830
Okay, calm down now.

03:35.830 --> 03:39.670
We may find it if we look for it,
and it's best not to get carried away.

03:40.130 --> 03:44.960
Agreed. Before we call the police,
we should probably search for it.

03:44.960 --> 03:46.210
Yes, exactly!

03:47.330 --> 03:48.380
A detective.

03:49.000 --> 03:49.540
Huh?

03:49.960 --> 03:51.460
Let's call a detective.

03:51.920 --> 03:52.630
What?

03:57.630 --> 04:00.330
Hmm, so this is the scene of the incident, eh?

04:00.330 --> 04:03.580
The stench of crime is pungent in here!

04:03.750 --> 04:08.000
She's starting something...
Oh, Koma-chan is the detective.

04:08.540 --> 04:11.250
Koma-chan also tends to have the time for this.

04:13.080 --> 04:17.210
Great Detective Koma will find the true culprit!

04:17.540 --> 04:19.000
I have time today!

04:21.630 --> 04:26.250
Originally, the word "detective"
was meant for the people doing investigations.

04:26.830 --> 04:33.250
In the Edo days, since the sergeants and constables
played the role of what we'd now call police officers,

04:33.080 --> 04:34.580
<b>Detectives</b>

04:33.250 --> 04:35.420
those people were also called "detectives."

04:35.920 --> 04:41.540
Wow, these days police officers and detectives
are totally different things, huh?

04:41.750 --> 04:44.880
When we moved into the Meiji era,
until private detectives started to appear,

04:44.880 --> 04:48.750
there were constables, and police detectives
were the ones called private detectives.

04:48.960 --> 04:50.130
Oh...

04:50.130 --> 04:52.460
They're so awesome, those detectives!

04:52.460 --> 04:56.250
I wanna be like "You're the criminal!" someday!

04:56.460 --> 05:00.790
Oh please, you just want to play detective
because you're bored, right?!

05:00.960 --> 05:02.790
Yeah, that's true.

05:03.880 --> 05:07.670
But I can't just ignore it
when Elda-sama is so distressed, can I?

05:08.920 --> 05:10.250
Koma-chan...

05:11.080 --> 05:11.960
Ba-dump!

05:12.540 --> 05:14.540
Stop suddenly turning into a hot guy.

05:15.920 --> 05:18.670
First of all, let's get the details straight
on the course of events of the incident.

05:19.710 --> 05:23.580
You realized the limited edition plastic model
was missing today, correct?

05:23.710 --> 05:24.880
Y-yes.

05:25.380 --> 05:30.580
Just as I was going to line up and play with the cool
plastic models that I've made up so far, it disappeared.

05:32.330 --> 05:36.630
<b>"It'd be so cool to line up all the</b>

05:33.460 --> 05:36.630
<b>plastic models I've made so far..."</b>

05:34.460 --> 05:36.630
<b>The elf murmured, to absolutely no one.</b>

05:37.250 --> 05:40.210
You organized your closet when you had that leak, right?

05:41.380 --> 05:45.540
C-come to think of it,
I don't think I saw it back then either.

05:48.170 --> 05:55.420
<b>"We've finally done about half of it.</b>

05:48.880 --> 05:55.420
<b>This is taking forever.</b>

05:49.420 --> 05:55.420
<b> When was the last time you organized this?"</b>

05:50.000 --> 05:55.420
<b> When the miko asked that, the elf unapologetically</b>

05:50.960 --> 05:55.420
<b>replied,</b>

05:51.170 --> 05:55.420
<b>"M-must be about 40 years ago, I think."</b>

05:51.750 --> 05:55.420
<b>As the miko felt the strength leave her body,</b>

05:52.920 --> 05:55.420
<b>she said in a thin voice,</b>

05:53.460 --> 05:55.420
<b>"That's why this is taking forever..."</b>

05:55.670 --> 05:58.170
Did you see it Koito?
Any idea about that limited edition plastic model?

05:58.290 --> 05:58.920
Huh?!

05:59.460 --> 06:03.920
Er, I didn't see it then... maybe?

06:04.580 --> 06:07.960
So basically at that point in time,
you think the plastic model was already gone...

06:08.500 --> 06:12.040
You're not looking too well, Koito. Are you all right?

06:12.290 --> 06:16.500
N-nah, that's not true! I'm feeling great! Yay!

06:18.500 --> 06:22.460
U-uh hey, what was
that limited edition plastic model like?

06:22.460 --> 06:24.960
Um... let me think.

06:27.920 --> 06:33.080
It looked just like this,
but it was made of a clearish transluscent plastic.

06:33.790 --> 06:36.380
Oh, so it was transluscent, huh?

06:38.130 --> 06:41.080
Could it be that you know where it is, Koito?

06:41.080 --> 06:42.750
Nope, no idea.

06:43.330 --> 06:46.880
You said it was transluscent,
but did it have little grains of something in it?

06:47.080 --> 06:50.630
Yes, it did. It had glitter in it,
and it looked like outer space.

06:51.630 --> 06:54.540
Koito, you know where it is after all, don't you?

06:54.540 --> 06:56.130
Nope, I have no clue.

06:56.920 --> 06:59.330
Okay! This investigation will take some legwork!

06:59.330 --> 07:01.330
Let's take a look outside your room, too!

07:02.960 --> 07:05.130
And thus, our investigation begins.

07:05.880 --> 07:10.000
We have no physical evidence,
nor do we have eyewitnesses.

07:08.250 --> 07:11.210
<b>Hinata</b>

07:08.250 --> 07:11.210
<b>Cake Flour</b>

07:14.210 --> 07:15.210
Huh?

07:16.500 --> 07:17.960
Where's the flour?

07:18.830 --> 07:21.000
The investigation proved to be a challenge...

07:22.420 --> 07:25.290
...however, step by step...

07:26.630 --> 07:31.040
I felt as if we were coming closer to the true culprit.

07:39.500 --> 07:41.830
Since the scene of the crime is the inner shrine,

07:41.830 --> 07:44.790
there is a high possiblity
that this is the criminal act of an inhabitant.

07:45.880 --> 07:47.170
The true culprit is...

07:48.250 --> 07:50.710
...among the people in Takamimi Shrine!

07:51.210 --> 07:53.080
Whaaaaaaat?!

07:53.080 --> 07:54.330
What...?

07:54.830 --> 08:02.000
Also, that person is one of the few who can come and go
from the reclusive and shy Elda-sama's room!

08:02.670 --> 08:05.170
The answer we can derive from that is...

08:08.920 --> 08:11.330
...Koito! You're the culprit!

08:11.330 --> 08:13.630
Wh-what did you say?!

08:22.750 --> 08:26.540
I did it! I'm sorry!

08:27.710 --> 08:31.580
It happened the day before
we tidied up your closet, Elda.

08:31.790 --> 08:35.580
I had carelessly stepped on a plastic model
that had fallen on the floor and broke it.

08:37.040 --> 08:43.170
<b>A stabbing pain assailed the miko.</b>

08:37.670 --> 08:43.170
<b>"Ouch!! Jeez, Elda is such a mess..."</b>

08:38.710 --> 08:43.170
<b>"Hm?"</b>

08:39.040 --> 08:43.170
<b>Laying at the miko's feet was a broken Gongem plastic model.</b>

08:40.210 --> 08:43.170
<b>"Uh oh..."</b>

08:40.710 --> 08:43.170
<b>A) "I have to tell Elda!"</b>

08:41.330 --> 08:43.170
<b>B) "I'll keep it secret from Elda and fix it!"</b>

08:42.080 --> 08:43.170
<b>C) "Man, I'm hungry..."</b>

08:43.250 --> 08:48.830
But it was only slightly broken,
so I planned to quietly fix it and bring it back...

08:50.500 --> 08:55.670
But it was harder than I thought it'd be.
It took a lot of time to fix it.

08:57.080 --> 09:00.750
<b>"I can fix this sort of thing really quickly."</b>

08:57.830 --> 09:00.750
<b>In high spirits, the miko grasped the Gongem's leg.</b>

08:58.790 --> 09:00.750
<b>"Huh? Does this part not bend this way?"</b>

08:59.710 --> 09:00.750
<b>"Huh?"</b>

09:00.960 --> 09:03.540
S-so that's what happened...

09:04.250 --> 09:07.880
I'm sorry, Elda!
But I treated it with care while I had it!

09:07.880 --> 09:11.000
I did my best to fix it, with Scotch tape!

09:11.960 --> 09:13.500
With Scotch tape?

09:14.420 --> 09:15.380
Yeah!

09:21.000 --> 09:21.670
Muh...

09:22.960 --> 09:31.540
My HG 1/144 Mobile Warrior Gongem
35th Anniversary Limited Clear Version!

09:24.630 --> 09:31.580
<b>HG 1/144 Mobile Warrior Gongem 35th Anniversary Limited Clear Version</b>

09:37.580 --> 09:43.710
We will now begin the trial of the case of the destruction
of Elda-sama's limited edition plastic model.

09:44.040 --> 09:47.040
What the hell is this? I'm in the middle of a house call.

09:47.380 --> 09:49.250
I'm in the middle of prep work.

09:49.500 --> 09:51.170
I'm busy.

09:51.170 --> 09:52.670
I'm busy!

09:52.670 --> 09:53.380
Silence!

09:54.040 --> 09:58.750
Aka-nee and Kado-chan,
as the adult representatives, will serve as jurors.

09:58.960 --> 09:59.750
What?!

09:59.750 --> 10:00.790
Jurors?!

10:01.500 --> 10:07.420
My precious plastic model went missing, right?
As I was searching for it, we started playing detective.

10:07.710 --> 10:10.170
Then it turned out that the culprit was Koito.

10:10.130 --> 10:12.710
<b>PERPETRATOR</b>

10:10.670 --> 10:14.880
And that's why I decided that we should also
hold a trial for Koito!

10:15.500 --> 10:17.420
After all, I have time today!

10:18.170 --> 10:22.130
Koma, you idiot! Adults don't have
enough free time to play court!

10:22.670 --> 10:26.960
Excuse me, Takamimi-sama.
Were there courthouses in the Edo Period?

10:27.380 --> 10:31.500
Of course there were.
They were... uhh... what was it again?

10:31.500 --> 10:34.080
I was talkin' to Takamimi-sama!

10:34.330 --> 10:35.880
I-I suppose they did...

10:36.000 --> 10:39.830
As for courthouses in the Edo days,
there were town magistrate's offices.

10:39.830 --> 10:42.040
Yeah, that's it! Magistrate's offices!

10:42.210 --> 10:46.710
It was like an office that combined city hall,
the police station, and the courthouse.

10:43.670 --> 10:45.380
<b>Magistrate's Office</b>

10:46.880 --> 10:48.630
<b>Government</b>

10:47.040 --> 10:51.960
Government, administration of justice, police,
all of it was handled by the magistrate's office.

10:50.500 --> 10:52.040
<b>Justice</b>

10:52.250 --> 10:56.080
The Detective that I told you about before
also belonged to the magistrate's office.

10:54.080 --> 10:55.960
<b>Police</b>

10:56.580 --> 11:03.170
<b>PERPETRATOR</b>

10:57.040 --> 11:01.920
The magistrate was a guy like
Toyama-no-Kin-san or Ooka Echizen, right?

11:02.040 --> 11:03.170
I know about them!

11:03.170 --> 11:08.580
Silence! Koito, you're the perpetrator
so you've gotta look way more miserable!

11:08.580 --> 11:10.000
F-fine...

11:10.830 --> 11:13.420
Now then, please present the evidence.

11:13.920 --> 11:15.710
H-here it is.

11:16.380 --> 11:20.380
Hmm, this toy that Takamimi-sama held dear to her...

11:20.380 --> 11:23.080
Koito-chan broke it... Is that what this is about?

11:23.580 --> 11:28.500
It was an extremely rare plastic model,
and now it's in this tragic state...

11:28.790 --> 11:31.420
Huh? But I fixed it up, didn't I?

11:31.830 --> 11:37.710
Choosing to put clear Scotch tape
on a clear plastic model is pretty sensible if you ask me.

11:31.960 --> 11:42.210
<b>PERPETRATOR</b>

11:38.130 --> 11:42.000
I'm sure there was an even bigger option called glue?!

11:43.330 --> 11:45.080
And what is the opinion of the jury?

11:46.670 --> 11:48.000
Hmm...

11:48.790 --> 11:51.630
I mean, isn't Takamimi-sama more at fault?

11:51.880 --> 11:52.500
Eh?

11:53.040 --> 11:56.080
Yeah. Koito is always working so hard.

11:56.080 --> 11:56.880
What?!

11:57.500 --> 12:00.630
Takamimi-sama is the reason
why it was so messy in the first place, right?

12:01.080 --> 12:04.670
There's nowhere to put your feet,
so it's inevitable that you'd step on a plastic model.

12:05.380 --> 12:09.080
It's also a bad idea to put such a precious thing
in a place where it might get stepped on.

12:10.080 --> 12:11.790
Th-this is true...

12:12.540 --> 12:18.290
Koito is always doing her best, and this may have been
caused by me not tidying up my room.

12:18.670 --> 12:21.500
Wait, Elda! It's actually all my fault!

12:22.130 --> 12:27.790
It's true that I'm the one who broke your plastic model...
and hiding it wasn't a good thing to do, no matter what.

12:28.920 --> 12:32.170
So Elda! I want you to give me a punishment!

12:32.500 --> 12:33.250
Huh?

12:34.210 --> 12:37.130
Indeed. Very sensible of you, Perpetrator.

12:37.330 --> 12:40.580
Now then, we shall leave the decision up to Elda-sama!

12:40.880 --> 12:45.330
Elda! Give me a severe punishment
so that I can forgive myself!

12:45.540 --> 12:46.670
Koito...

12:48.040 --> 12:50.210
I understand how you feel very well!

12:51.170 --> 12:55.540
In order for Koito to comprehend
the significance of the Gongem she broke...

12:56.710 --> 13:04.170
<b>Mobile Warrior</b>

12:56.710 --> 13:04.170
<b>Gongem</b>

12:58.830 --> 13:01.080
she will watch all 43 episodes

13:01.080 --> 13:03.790
of the first Mobile Warrior Gongem series with me!

13:05.500 --> 13:08.580
I am utterly uninterested,
but this is a punishment, after all.

13:09.580 --> 13:10.250
Okay!

13:10.880 --> 13:15.250
Good! And with this, court is adjourned!
Because it didn't turn out to be very interesting at all!

13:15.380 --> 13:18.670
I thought it'd help kill a little more time!

13:20.540 --> 13:23.500
If you've got that much free time,
come help out at my shop.

13:23.500 --> 13:27.500
I'm coming down there to drink later,
so put some hard work in there, idiot Koma!

13:27.750 --> 13:28.960
Eh?

13:37.670 --> 13:40.830
Yes, episode 34 was great, right?!

13:41.130 --> 13:44.540
Next up is episode 35, which is basically scenes
cut from the movie version,

13:44.540 --> 13:47.500
so though there are a lot of scenes
that you can't see in the TV series,

13:47.500 --> 13:49.040
but even among those scenes the focus is-

13:55.000 --> 13:59.960
<b>YUMIMIMI</b>

13:55.000 --> 13:59.960
<b>FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

13:59.960 --> 14:02.920
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

14:03.330 --> 14:08.330
We've got quite the event to look forward
to this year as well... The Yumimimi Festival.

14:08.630 --> 14:12.830
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

14:08.630 --> 14:12.830
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL</b>

14:09.380 --> 14:12.750
Everyone in Tsukishima is already
all caught up in the festivals.

14:12.830 --> 14:14.330
<b>YUMIMIMI FESTIVAL!</b>

14:14.540 --> 14:17.500
Well, there is one more week until the Yumimimi Festival.

14:18.170 --> 14:23.460
We can't stay together this time since I'll be helping
Grampa, so you'll be okay on your own, right?

14:23.630 --> 14:29.750
Of course I will! This is your first Yumimimi Festival
since you became a miko, so I have to do my best!

14:30.080 --> 14:31.750
That's some amazing motivation there!

14:31.750 --> 14:34.380
You always hate doing
the major rituals, what's going on?

14:35.630 --> 14:37.750
You mustn't underestimate me, dear miko.

14:38.580 --> 14:43.290
Just going once around Tsukishima on the portable
shrine for the Yumimimi Festival is a piece of cake.

14:43.920 --> 14:47.250
That's the informal ritual, right? Didn't Gramps tell you?

14:47.500 --> 14:49.420
We're doing the Oyumi ritual as well this year.

14:49.500 --> 14:51.670
Huh? The thing where I'm on a boat?

14:51.960 --> 14:55.250
Yup! That was an informal thing
since there was no miko the whole time.

14:55.580 --> 14:59.790
They say they're doing it up big this year,
and even the parishioners are pulling out all the stops!

15:00.040 --> 15:03.040
Th-then I don't wanna do it.

15:04.210 --> 15:07.960
B-but see, you're the foundation,
and you just have to ride the boat!

15:08.380 --> 15:11.080
You won't be going up anything high,
so it's not scary, right?

15:11.290 --> 15:13.380
Obviously the boat is scary, too!

15:13.500 --> 15:15.630
In the end, I'm the one doing it, you know!

15:15.670 --> 15:17.630
Don't snap at me pathetically like that.

15:18.960 --> 15:25.380
The Yumimimi Festival is Takamimi Shrine's festival,
where we pray for peace at sea.

15:26.210 --> 15:29.000
The highlight of the event is,
without a doubt, the Oyumi ritual!

15:30.000 --> 15:33.630
The practice of the head priest shooting an arrow
aboard a boat on the Sumida River

15:34.080 --> 15:38.630
is an essential ritual to predict whether or not
that year will have a good fishing haul.

15:40.080 --> 15:44.920
Well, since I'm helping out this time around,
it'll be easy street for me.

15:41.500 --> 15:49.630
<b>Helper</b>

15:45.130 --> 15:49.630
<b>Major Role</b>

15:45.170 --> 15:49.710
Th-that's not fair, Koito! The enshrined deity
and the miko should be together until the grave!

15:50.000 --> 15:52.170
At least say we're bound together by destiny.

15:53.420 --> 15:58.290
Let's see... here's the bow and arrow
used to drive off evil in the Oyumi ritual.

15:58.790 --> 16:00.460
Is this the target you'll have, Elda?

16:01.130 --> 16:06.710
Yes. The archer will shoot the arrow three times, and the
closer to the center of the target, the better the catch.

16:07.080 --> 16:10.210
If it misses entirely, it means "maybe next year."

16:07.830 --> 16:11.540
<b>Good</b>

16:07.830 --> 16:11.540
<b>haul</b>

16:08.830 --> 16:11.540
<b>Fairly</b>

16:08.830 --> 16:11.540
<b>good</b>

16:09.580 --> 16:11.540
<b>Normal</b>

16:10.080 --> 16:11.540
<b>Maybe</b>

16:10.080 --> 16:11.540
<b>next</b>

16:10.090 --> 16:11.540
<b>year...</b>

16:11.670 --> 16:13.630
Not sure I should ask this, but...

16:13.790 --> 16:16.460
Is it possible to shoot an enshrined deity
with an arrow in a ritual?

16:16.460 --> 16:19.540
Oh, yes. I mean, the tip has a suction cup on it.

16:20.130 --> 16:27.040
Well, of course in the Edo days, I was the archer.
I shot at a target that the head priest was holding.

16:27.330 --> 16:30.540
What? I didn't know you could use a bow and arrow!

16:30.540 --> 16:34.250
Y-yeah. We elves are quite skilled at it,
the bow and arrow.

16:34.630 --> 16:39.080
But when I focused on the bow,
I lost my footing and fell in the sea.

16:39.210 --> 16:42.580
Before I was summoned here,
I lived in a land-locked area.

16:41.920 --> 16:44.830
<b>ABABABABABA!</b>

16:41.920 --> 16:44.830
<b>ABABABABABA!</b>

16:41.920 --> 16:44.830
<b>ABABABABABA!</b>

16:41.920 --> 16:44.830
<b>ABABABABABA!</b>

16:41.920 --> 16:44.830
<b>ABABABABABA!</b>

16:42.580 --> 16:44.210
I really freaked out!

16:44.830 --> 16:52.670
<b>I don't want to get on!</b>

16:44.830 --> 16:52.670
<b>I don't want to get on!</b>

16:44.840 --> 16:52.670
<b>I don't want to get on!</b>

16:44.840 --> 16:52.670
<b>I don't want to get on!</b>

16:44.840 --> 16:52.670
<b>I don't want to get on!</b>

16:44.920 --> 16:52.670
I don't want to get on! I don't want to get on! I don't want to get on!

16:45.500 --> 16:50.040
So, at the next Oyumi ritual I threw a tantrum
and said I didn't want to get on the boat.

16:50.540 --> 16:52.250
I can absolutely see that happening.

16:52.750 --> 16:56.170
But for some reason that year
the fishing haul was super bountiful.

16:56.380 --> 17:00.580
A rumor spread that we had a great haul
because I fell into the water.

17:01.790 --> 17:04.000
I've heard that rumor before as well!

17:04.420 --> 17:08.250
Since then, I somehow feel like I'm expected to fall...

17:09.460 --> 17:12.330
Would you rather make it a ritual
where you dive into the river?

17:12.670 --> 17:14.790
You're misunderstanding the priorities here.

17:16.500 --> 17:20.880
But if it really is true that you falling in the water
was the cause of a great haul, that would be awesome.

17:21.080 --> 17:26.080
I'm just a simple elf, and I don't have
any sort of divine power like that.

17:26.460 --> 17:30.630
Ah! Could it be that you have a smell
that fish like or something?!

17:30.290 --> 17:35.250
<b>What is this aroma...?!</b>

17:31.170 --> 17:34.920
S-saying your deity smells like fish bait
is something you just do not do!

17:35.960 --> 17:37.170
Here you go.

17:38.080 --> 17:39.630
Th-thanks.

17:40.170 --> 17:43.750
I'm done checking the ritual articles,
so all that's left is to wait for everything to start!

17:45.330 --> 17:47.920
Boats are scary... Water is scary...

17:48.170 --> 17:53.540
Grampa is an expert in archery, and you'll be on
a big boat so there's nothing to worry about!

17:53.540 --> 17:56.540
Y-you're right... you're very right.

17:57.000 --> 17:57.540
Yeah.

17:57.920 --> 18:00.000
Way back then, this was done in the sea,

18:00.000 --> 18:02.710
but since it'll be in the Sumida River now,
the boat should hardly sway at all.

18:03.130 --> 18:04.790
Around where will I be doing this again?

18:05.250 --> 18:06.580
Um, let's see...

18:08.080 --> 18:14.500
They said it was by the Kachidoki Bridge
behind our house so... I think it's around here.

18:14.750 --> 18:19.460
O-oh, okay. There'll definitely be
a lot of people there, huh?

18:19.460 --> 18:21.210
Well, yeah, it is a festival, you know.

18:22.330 --> 18:27.380
When I look at the map again like this,
Tokyo surprisingly has a lot of rivers.

18:27.830 --> 18:32.420
Yes... Well, there's quite a few less
compared to Edo times.

18:32.830 --> 18:35.250
They've become culverts and roads and the like.

18:35.540 --> 18:39.380
Really? Then in the past
there were even more rivers everywhere?

18:39.920 --> 18:45.500
Yeah. Edo was originally a desolate land
with far-reaching thickets and marshes.

18:46.000 --> 18:50.130
The first thing Ieyasu-kun did
when he arrived in Edo was construction

18:50.130 --> 18:53.420
to spruce up the rivers
and make them easier to use as canals.

18:53.960 --> 18:59.290
Daily necessities, lumber, and foodstuff
that were sent to Edo from all over Japan,

18:59.460 --> 19:02.750
and were carried all over the place using the waterways.

19:03.460 --> 19:04.920
Ooh...

19:05.290 --> 19:06.460
According to Ieyasu-kun,

19:06.460 --> 19:12.920
Edo grew into a large city precisely because
of the infrastructural development of the canal.

19:13.500 --> 19:17.630
Wow, Lord Ieyasu really was an outstanding person.

19:17.880 --> 19:32.210
<b>Mayor, we have a problem! The city is flooding.</b>

19:17.880 --> 19:32.210
<b>It seems that if you keep the coastline clear,</b>

19:17.880 --> 19:32.210
<b>you're less likely to have flooding.</b>

19:20.250 --> 19:26.960
I also tried to copy him and build a city of canals
in Sim City, but it was immediately destroyed by floods.

19:26.960 --> 19:29.420
I realized Ieyasu-kun was amazing.

19:29.630 --> 19:31.750
Your scale for respect
is at an elementary school level, huh...?

19:32.210 --> 19:37.920
<b>OYUMI RITUAL - RITUAL ARTICLES</b>

19:33.250 --> 19:37.540
The most recent Oyumi ritual
was more than ten years ago, right?

19:37.920 --> 19:41.210
I think I remember watching it
from the river bank when I was small, though.

19:41.580 --> 19:45.420
That's right. I was scared to ride the boat back then, too.

19:45.920 --> 19:49.210
How was it then? What were the results with the bow?

19:49.420 --> 19:51.130
Um, actually...

19:52.500 --> 19:54.790
The first shot was "normal,"

19:58.920 --> 20:00.790
the second shot was "fairly good,"

20:03.080 --> 20:10.540
<b>Excitement</b>

20:03.080 --> 20:10.540
<b>Anxiety</b>

20:03.090 --> 20:10.540
<b>Anxiety</b>

20:03.090 --> 20:10.540
<b>Excitement</b>

20:03.090 --> 20:10.540
<b>Anxiety</b>

20:03.420 --> 20:06.830
and when all the parishioners truly expected
that with the way things were going,

20:06.830 --> 20:10.380
I'd get it smack dab in the middle the third time...

20:12.210 --> 20:14.750
The third shot was "maybe next year."

20:17.880 --> 20:22.330
Well, that in itself kind of felt like a punchline
was delivered, and it was funny, though.

20:23.670 --> 20:26.790
So that's what happened.
But Gramps is really good at using the bow.

20:27.170 --> 20:28.630
Oh, at that time...

20:29.500 --> 20:33.080
Gramps doesn't look like it,
but he can be careless sometimes.

20:33.880 --> 20:35.960
That's absolutely true.

20:36.630 --> 20:42.960
Speaking of, didn't you learn archery, Koito?
Haven't the Koganei children studied it for generations?

20:43.290 --> 20:46.000
Grampa doesn't like stuff like traditions.

20:46.420 --> 20:50.170
I run track, and Koyuzu attetnds a cooking class.

20:50.420 --> 20:52.880
Th-that's true, now that you mention it.

20:53.420 --> 20:54.960
But here's the truth.

20:55.210 --> 21:00.130
I kind of wanted to give it try, too.
I wanted to do the Oyumi ritual with you, Elda.

21:00.750 --> 21:01.920
Is that so?

21:02.210 --> 21:08.290
<b>OYUMI RITUAL - RITUAL ARTICLES</b>

21:02.580 --> 21:05.330
Despite how things look,
I am Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto's miko.

21:05.790 --> 21:07.880
But I have no experience with archery,

21:08.290 --> 21:11.080
and it's not something I can learn in a single day.

21:11.750 --> 21:14.420
Then would you like to give it try just once, right now?

21:14.420 --> 21:15.080
Huh?

21:15.630 --> 21:20.500
We're in the precincts, and I'm going to hold the target
so it's okay if you shoot the arrow.

21:20.500 --> 21:21.750
Uh, are you sure?

21:23.290 --> 21:26.880
I might hit the middle of your foreheard
instead of the target.

21:26.880 --> 21:29.330
I-I would like it if you wouldn't joke like that...

21:29.670 --> 21:32.130
It's more difficult than you think, I'm sure.

21:40.420 --> 21:43.330
Were you aiming for a headshot?! Were you?!

21:43.330 --> 21:46.880
N-no! It just went that way when I aimed for the target!

21:46.960 --> 21:48.500
O-okay...

21:49.170 --> 21:52.880
I should leave the Oyumi ritual to Grampa after all.

21:53.420 --> 21:57.420
S-Sis, Elda-sama! W-we've got a problem!

21:57.420 --> 21:59.790
Wh-what is it, Koyuzu? What's wrong?

22:00.130 --> 22:05.880
I just got a message.
Grampa got hurt getting the scaffolding ready!

22:06.040 --> 22:06.830
What?!

22:06.960 --> 22:08.580
I-is he okay?!

22:08.830 --> 22:11.460
It seems like the wound itself isn't anything major,

22:12.210 --> 22:15.460
but he sprained his wrist and it'll take 3 weeks
to make a full recovery, they said.

22:15.670 --> 22:18.380
O-oh man, that's a relief!

22:18.630 --> 22:20.790
Just a sprained wrist, huh?

22:22.920 --> 22:25.630
Wrist... 3 weeks to recover?

22:26.000 --> 22:28.420
The Yumimimi Festival is next week, isn't it?

22:26.710 --> 22:28.540
<b>3 weeks * Next week</b>

22:29.790 --> 22:33.380
Yeah. So he told you to be the archer, Sis.

22:38.500 --> 22:42.380
I don't like headshots! No headshots!
